corrective_lesson:incident:evidence_unavailable
The operation timed out before a result was recorded, so its true outcome is unknown. Recording this as a failure would convert missing evidence into a verdict, which is exactly the mistake to avoid. Obtain an authoritative record of the operation's outcome before accepting or rejecting the result; a missing answer must not be recorded as either success or failure.
